 McGill","x":"…about that, I guess, is now that that's come down a bit the 95.8% a valid point between physical and economic, but do you start to think about pricing power getting back to pre-pandemic levels here then pretty soon since that's a bit below occupancy where you were in the fourth quarter 2019.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"CPT 2022 Q3","e":"cpt","d":"2022-10-28","l":"cost_cuts","r":"analyst","s":"Ric Campo","x":"…is -- and I also think that we'll be able to shorten our development time frame, which will take cost out of it -- out of the system with fewer developments getting done rather, than having to add time to the scheduling might be able to take some time out of the schedule, and compress that to…","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"CPT 2022 Q3","e":"cpt","d":"2022-10-28","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Keith Oden","x":"Our performance was in line with our expectations, so we've maintained our outlook for 2022 full year revenue growth of 11.25% at the midpoint of our guidance range.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"CPT 2022 Q3","e":"cpt","d":"2022-10-28","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Keith Oden","x":"Actually, raised the guidance $0.01 for the full year.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"CPT 2022 Q4","e":"cpt","d":"2023-02-03","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Keith Oden","x":"Given recent announcements regarding layoffs in the technology sector, we will keep an eye on both of these markets for any future signs of slowing demand.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"CPT 2022 Q4","e":"cpt","d":"2023-02-03","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Alex Jessett","x":"The remaining 57% of our operating expenses are anticipated to grow at approximately 4% as inflation and wage pressures combined with anticipated increases in marketing expenses as we face increased supply are partially offset by the positive impact of our 2022 on-site staff restructuring.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"CPT 2022 Q4","e":"cpt","d":"2023-02-03","l":"guidance","r":"analyst","s":"Ric Campo","x":"We exceeded the top end of our guidance and raised guidance every quarter.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"CPT 2023 Q1","e":"cpt","d":"2023-04-28","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Alexander Jessett","x":"…adjustments we make to drive core FFO, which primarily are unusual or large casualty events, severance charges in 2022 related to changes to our on-site staffing model and the amortization, if any, of below or above market leases associated with acquisitions will also be adjusted from our…","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"CPT 2023 Q1","e":"cpt","d":"2023-04-28","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Alexander Jessett","x":"…this original guidance was approximately $900,000 of first quarter 2022 revenue associated with the amortization of below-market leases from previously acquired communities and approximately $900,000 of first quarter 2022 severance costs associated with changes to our on-site staffing model.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"CPT 2023 Q2","e":"cpt","d":"2023-08-04","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Alex Jessett","x":"Remember also that we did increase guidance in the first quarter.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"CPT 2023 Q2","e":"cpt","d":"2023-08-04","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Alex Jessett","x":"But so as compared to what we thought when we last increased guidance everything is progressing as we expected.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"CPT 2023 Q3","e":"cpt","d":"2023-10-27","